        "original_id": "fb0c7dbf-f35d-5cfd-a190-c1541ea24e38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport, Rickenbacker International Airport, San Juan, Carolina, Columbus, Lockbourne, Franklin County, Ohio, Puerto Rico\n- Organizations: Pro-Air Services, WZIN\n- Roles: airport, civil-military airport, air charter operator, radio station\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is a joint civil-military international airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is also known as Aeropuerto Internacional Luis Muñoz Marín and Isla Verde International Airport.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Luis Muñoz Marín, Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor.\n- Rickenbacker International Airport is a civil-military public airport 10 miles south of downtown Columbus near Lockbourne in southern Franklin County, Ohio.\n- Pro-Air Services is an air charter operator based at Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport in San Juan, Puerto Rico.\n- WZIN serves San Juan, Puerto Rico, and the entire metropolitan area.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
